                                    <h1>Supply Chain Management Software: India &amp; UAE Guide 2026</h1>
                                    <p>Supply chain became a boardroom-level topic after 2020 — and stayed there. Building or selecting SCM software correctly is now a multi-year strategic decision. Here is a practical guide to the SCM landscape in 2026, with focus on India-to-UAE and multi-country operations.</p>
                                    <h2>What SCM Software Actually Covers</h2>
                                    <p>1. S&OP (sales & operations planning)<br>2. Demand forecasting<br>3. Procurement + supplier management<br>4. Inventory optimization<br>5. Warehouse + logistics execution<br>6. Transportation management (TMS)<br>7. Order fulfillment<br>8. Supply chain visibility + control tower</p>
                                    <h2>Off-Shelf Options</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Enterprise:</strong> SAP IBP + SAP TM + SAP EWM, Oracle SCM Cloud, Blue Yonder (formerly JDA), Kinaxis. $500K-5M+/year.<br><strong>Mid-market:</strong> Infor Nexus, e2open, o9 Solutions, Coupa. $100K-1M/year.<br><strong>India-first:</strong> Increff, Vinculum, Unicommerce. ₹15 lakh - 2 Cr/year.<br><strong>UAE-friendly:</strong> Same as global. IBM Sterling, Infor SCM, Blue Yonder all strong locally.</p>
                                    <h2>When Custom SCM Makes Sense</h2>
                                    <p>Rare — but real. Categories that justify custom: highly regulated (pharma cold chain), unique operational models (jewelry, high-value logistics), and companies with 5+ years of process refinement worth codifying.</p>
                                    <h2>Cross-Border India → UAE Ops</h2>
                                    <p>The specific scenario we build for: India-manufactured D2C brand shipping to UAE + GCC. Requires: multi-warehouse allocation (India + UAE), duty / VAT calculation at order time, cross-border logistics coordination (Aramex, DHL, DSV), UAE-specific customs handling, and reverse-logistics for returns. Custom or heavily-configured SCM required — off-shelf tools rarely handle the nuance.</p>
                                    <h2>Demand Forecasting: The Highest-ROI SCM Investment</h2>
                                    <p>Accurate demand forecasting drives inventory optimization (10-25% inventory reduction), stockout reduction (15-30% fewer OOS events), and better supplier relationships (fewer expedited orders). Modern approach: ML-based forecasting with weekly or daily updates, per-SKU per-location.</p>
                                    <h2>Cost + Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>SaaS integration:</strong> ₹25-90 lakh / $30K-108K over 12-24 weeks.<br><strong>Custom SCM module builds:</strong> ₹75 lakh - 3 Cr / $90K-360K, 20-40 weeks.<br><strong>Enterprise multi-module deployment:</strong> ₹3-15 Cr / $360K-1.8M over 12-36 months.</p>

